### Critical: [conftest.py](file:///e:/03-Code/Projects/Legacy/DocsSense/backend/tests/conftest.py)

The conftest executes a precise 7-step patching sequence **at module scope** (not inside fixtures) to handle the backend's import-time side effects:

```
STEP 1: os.environ["REDIS_URL"] = ...       → Prevents ValueError in redis_repo_sync
STEP 2: Import mock classes                   → Pure Python, no app deps
STEP 3: redis.from_url = FakeSyncRedis       → Patches sync + async Redis constructors
STEP 4: SentenceTransformer = FakeModel      → Prevents 80MB model download
STEP 5: chromadb.CloudClient = MockChroma    → Prevents ChromaDB Cloud API calls
STEP 6: from main import app                  → NOW SAFE — all side effects intercepted
STEP 7: celery_app.conf.update(eager=True)   → Tasks run synchronously in-process
```

